 instant-character
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both 90s attempts were hitting concurrent.futures.TimeoutError (empty
error string). Portrait generation runs in a daemon thread already so
there is no Railway HTTP timeout risk — fal.subscribe can block as long
as the model needs. Stripped the executor wrapper entirely and call
fal.subscribe directly. Added repr() to error log so silent exceptions
(TimeoutError, etc.) print their type.

